;; §8B.4 oracle-answer pinning (docs/incremental.md; docs/smt.md §7): base
;; program for the session regression.  It declares the shape only -- the
;; battery drives every input through tip batches, because the FIRST flush
;; is itself a pin: against an EMPTY answer table, certification must
;; refuse counted routes (oracle-fallback), since a demand first raised
;; under a maintenance flavor (which registers no oracle bindings) would
;; never dispatch.  The later deletion pins answer persistence: a rerun
;; must PRESERVE the answer table, because a cleared answer can never come
;; back -- the re-derived demand struct resurrects its interned id, which
;; the oracle registry's persistent answered set skips.
include "../../lib/smt.slog"

table (input int)
table (keep int)

rule
(input X)
(= (sat) (smt_check (llt (ic X) (ic 5))))
-->
(keep X)
